Subject: [PATCH] shell: load the Nulavio Horizon theme in the browser window

The main window loads no branding stylesheet, so a product theme would
otherwise need userChrome.css (a per-profile, user-level file) or an
add-on that styles the window after it appears. One stylesheet link,
loaded after every upstream sheet, lets the theme re-value upstream
design tokens from the first paint. The stylesheet lives in the Nulavio
branding directory; everything it changes is documented there.

Owner: Nulavio maintainers
Upstream: not applicable (product theme).
---
--- a/browser/base/content/browser.xhtml
+++ b/browser/base/content/browser.xhtml
@@ -57,6 +57,9 @@
     rel="stylesheet"
     href="chrome://global/content/resistfingerprinting/letterboxing.css"
   />
+  <!-- Nulavio Horizon window theme: loaded last, re-values design tokens
+       (browser/branding/nulavio/content/theme/horizon.css). -->
+  <link rel="stylesheet" href="chrome://branding/content/theme/horizon.css" />
 
   <link rel="localization" href="branding/brand.ftl"/>
   <link rel="localization" href="browser/allTabsMenu.ftl"/>
